DESCRIPTION:Carol Gail Lee\, 83\, of Marceline\, Missouri\, passed away pe
 acefully on Friday August 7\, 2026. Carol was born on May 6\, 1943\, in Br
 ashear\, Missouri\, to Rev. G.D. Hammontree and Bonnie Lee (Sullins) Hammo
 ntree. She spent her life devoted to her family and her Christian faith. O
 n June 9\, 1963\, Carol married the love of her life\, John Steven Lee. To
 gether they shared 63 years of marriage. Carol attended college and worked
  as a bookkeeper throughout her career. She was a faithful member of First
  Baptist Church\, where her faith served as a guiding light throughout her
  life. She is survived by her beloved husband\, John Steven Lee\; her son\
 , Nicholas Venneman (Shelby Stafford) of Chillicothe\, Missouri\; her daug
 hter\, Chelsey Venneman (Malachi Philips-Bey) of Marceline\, Missouri\; he
 r cherished grandchildren\, Jace Wills and Oaklee Venneman\; and her siste
 r\, Joann Foster\; and her twin brother\, G. Dale Hammontree (Ruth Hammont
 ree). Carol was preceded in death by her daughter\, Kristi Renee Lee\; her
  parents\, Rev. G.D. Hammontree and Bonnie Lee Hammontree\; her sisters\, 
 Peggy Payne and Helen Minor\; her brothers-in-law\, D. L. Payne\, Frank Fo
 ster\, and Robert E. Lee\; and her parents-in-law\, Eugene Lee and Mary Et
 hlyne Lee. A visitation will be held on Tuesday\, August 11\, 2026\, begin
 ning at 2:00 p.m.\, followed by a memorial service at 3:00 p.m. at the Fir
 st Baptist Church in Marceline\, Missouri. Psalm 23 The LORD Is My Shepher
 d A Psalm of David. [1] The LORD is my shepherd\; I shall not want. [2]  H
 e makes me lie down in green pastures. He leads me beside still waters. [3
 ]  He restores my soul. He leads me in paths of righteousness for his name
 ’s sake. [4] Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of deat
 h\, I will fear no evil\, for you are with me\; your rod and your staff\, 
 they comfort me. [5] You prepare a table before me in the presence of my e
 nemies\; you anoint my head with oil\; my cup overflows. [6] Surely goodne
 ss and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life\, and I shall dwell i
 n the house of the LORD forever. (ESV)\n\nFull obituary and service detail
 s: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obituaries/Carol-Gail-Lee?obId=49204
 775
LOCATION:Marceline\, MO
END:VEVENT
